From 4883d53ceaa7481e3c5c796df44e872aa0381a66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael E <michaele@intel.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:43:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ethernet: INTERNAL: e1000e: fix TX hang after failed S4
 hibernate cycle

When hibernation fails (e.g. "Swap header not found!"), the
freeze/thaw cycle leaves the e1000e adapter in a broken state:
the PHY Reset Asserted (PHYRA) bit remains set in the MAC Status
register, preventing TX descriptor processing. The watchdog then
detects "Hardware Unit Hang" every 2 seconds indefinitely because
e1000_print_hw_hang() only logs the error without scheduling a
recovery reset.

To fix:

In e1000e_pm_thaw(), call e1000e_reset() before e1000e_up()
to clear stale hardware state (including PHYRA) after the
freeze/thaw cycle. This matches the resume path which already
calls e1000e_reset() in __e1000_resume().

Signed-off-by: Michael E <michaele@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000e/netdev.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000e/netdev.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000e/netdev.c
index 60fc62794c7b..cddb43392859 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000e/netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000e/netdev.c
@@ -6904,6 +6904,11 @@ static int e1000e_pm_thaw(struct device *dev)
 
 	rtnl_lock();
 	if (netif_running(netdev)) {
+		/* Reset adapter to clear stale PHY state (e.g. PHYRA)
+		 * after freeze/thaw cycle. Without this,
+		 * a failed hibernation leaves the TX path hung.
+		 */
+		e1000e_reset(adapter);
 		rc = e1000_request_irq(adapter);
 		if (rc)
 			goto err_irq;
-- 
2.43.0

